<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Highcrest handling for base-game (GTA) cars.

  How to add a car:
  1. Tune it in game with /handlingeditor and export.
  2. Paste the exported <Item type="CHandlingData"> ... </Item> block below, between
     <HandlingData> and </HandlingData>. One block per car.
  3. The <handlingName> must match the car's handling name (usually its model name in
     capitals, e.g. SULTAN, ELEGY2, KURUMA).
  4. Upload, restart the server, and players fully reopen FiveM.

  Add-on cars (their own resource folder) keep their handling in their own handling.meta:
  replace that car's <Item> there instead of adding it here.
-->
<CHandlingDataMgr>
  <HandlingData>

  </HandlingData>
</CHandlingDataMgr>
